Hi Mihoko and Patrick,

Mihoko and I have finished aligning the prompts for the Japanese and US sessi=
ons. In our July 10 internal read-through we worked through 18 questions and =
removed five that supplied the answer or assumed a confirmation. The remainin=
g 13 are in the same order in both languages in the attached comparison.

The shared interview frame is 45 minutes: 5 for the opening, 7 for recall, 10=
 for state and reason, 10 for change and cross-checking, 10 for passing infor=
mation on, and 3 to close. The read-through took 51 minutes including our sto=
ps to reconsider wording; it was a preparation exercise, not a participant ti=
ming result.

Please let the participant use their own terms before offering any translatio=
n or label. Record the words they use, even when they differ from ours, and f=
ollow their account of what was checked and passed on. If they have already a=
nswered a prompt, confirm the essential point rather than asking it again in =
full.

Thanks,
Jennifer

